{"user": "Why are corners so important?", "user_ts": "2026-08-07T13:14:28.819026+00:00", "assistant": "Corners are important because **a disc in a corner can never be flipped**\u2014there\u2019s no square beyond it to outflank it. Once you own a corner like **h1** or **a8**, the edge discs connected to it often become safe too.\n\nThat\u2019s why squares next to corners can be dangerous: playing near **h1** (like **g2**) may let White take **h1**, giving them permanent discs and edge control. In the endgame, that can matter more than the flips you get immediately.", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-07T13:14:31.730632+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-07T13:14:33.875223+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "consensus": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "votes": {"Knowledge Deficit Question": 3}, "confidence": {"Knowledge Deficit Question": 1.0}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "llama": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "sonnet": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant": {"final": ["Direct Instruction"], "consensus": ["Direct Instruction"], "votes": {"Direct Instruction": 3, "Hint": 1}, "confidence": {"Direct Instruction": 1.0, "Hint": 0.3333333333333333}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Direct Instruction"], "llama": ["Direct Instruction", "Hint"], "sonnet": ["Direct Instruction"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant_fine": {"final": ["Local Justification", "General Principle"], "consensus": ["Local Justification", "General Principle"], "votes": {"Local Justification": 3, "General Principle": 3, "Worked Line": 1}, "confidence": {"Local Justification": 1.0, "General Principle": 1.0, "Worked Line": 0.3333333333333333}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Local Justification", "General Principle"], "llama": ["Local Justification", "Worked Line", "G